! Experimental and kinetic modeling studies on high-pressure oxidation of RP-3 surrogate fuel. Part Ⅰ: Three-stage oxidation phenomenon of a three-component surrogate fuel
! Xiang Gao, Du Wang, Qian-Peng Wang, Xu-Peng Yu, Ya-Ning Zhang, Zhen-Yu Tian*
! tianzhenyu@iet.cn
! Thermodata
!#the Plog and Chebyshev rate expressions, only available for Chemkin(Java) version >4.0, Cantera version>2.0, Opensmoke or CHEMKIN-II with P-plog interpreter.!
!#some of lumped reaction from Polimi mechanism may increase the stiffness of the mechanism lead to the converge problem!
!#the chebyshev rate experssions may lead to the converge problem and should note their pressure and temperature range!
! INSTRUCTIONS TO USE THE MODEL:
! 1) SEARCH FOR 'MAIN BATH' TO COMMENT OUT THE APPROPRIATE EXPRESSION
!    FOR H+O2(+M)<=>HO2(+M), DEPENDING ON THE USER SPECIFIED BATH GAS, "M".
! 2) REACTIONS WHOSE RATE CONSTANTS DEPEND ON PRESSURE BUT WHICH HAVE NO TROE OR LINDEMAN FORMALISM ARE GROUPED
!    AND LISTED AT THE END OF THE FILE. PICK THE BLOCK THAT BEST SATISFY THE CHOSEN CONDITIONS.

